    },
    {
      "level": "h6",
      "font": "space-grotesk",
      "heading": "THE CYCLE\n",
      "_template": "header"
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "A fallen organism nourishes another. A surface becomes a home. A body becomes a landscape. Life grows over life, again and again, quietly reshaping what already exists.\n\nThis installation imagines that continuous process of becoming.\n",
      "_template": "header"
    },
    {
      "width": "full",
      "images": [
        {
          "src": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dkxfwnlbz/image/upload/v1783505050/5_r8mckh.jpg"
        }
      ],
      "_template": "image"
    },
    {
      "level": "h6",
      "font": "space-grotesk",
      "heading": "THE WITNESS\n",
      "_template": "header"
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "font": "sedan",
      "heading": "The tree stands as a witness to time. It carries the memory of countless lives that have appeared, disappeared, and returned in new forms. As organisms emerge from its surface, they do not merely grow on the tree—they gradually redefine it. With every new layer, every new species, every new trace of life, the tree itself becomes something different.\n",
      "_template": "header"
    },
    {
      "width": "narrow",
      "images": [
        {
